module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.memo_key_cost_proportional_to_argument_size

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data memo_key_cost_proportional_to_argument_size: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "memo_key_cost_proportional_to_argument_size" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a memo that keys every call by the content of its arguments derives that key at a cost proportional to the arguments' size, on every call, including calls that can never recur. A recursion threading one large value through its steps then pays O(|value|) per step and O(|value|^2) in total, and the cost lands on whichever program happens to thread a large value, not on the provider that charged it.",
    "HARM: extdeps.languages.json parse_json_document was reported as not returning on a large document and was read as a parser defect. The parser is linear with the memo off; the cost was the interpreter's default-on eval-call memo (v1_interpreter eval_pure_named_call -> eval_recompute_key). A cost defect in a shared provider presents as a defect in its most visible consumer, which is how a victim gets repaired instead of the cause.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: the instrument is tools.json_parse_ladder (dag/gunbc/instruments/json_parse_ladder.dag), one `gunbc run --function <rung>` per rung, each rung exiting non-zero when its value is not the one it owes. The discriminator is GUNBC_EVAL_MEMO=0, the memo's declared diagnostic realization switch with identical values: a curve that bends with the memo on and runs linear with it off locates the cost in the key and not in the consumer. A recursion that only PASSES the value, never reading it, paying the whole cost is the second tell; holding the same value in scope without passing it pays nothing.",
    "TWO INSTANCES, ONE CLASS. (1) A String argument was hashed in full per call because strings bypassed the identity hash memo that composites use: CLOSED by gunbc#12065, RcStr carries its content hash once per lineage (v1.compiler.runtime_rust rt_string_carrier), key values unchanged, re-serialized documents byte-identical. (2) A freshly built accumulator argument -- a list_push result, a new Rc every step -- misses the identity hash memo on every call and is rehashed in full: OPEN, and it cannot close at a carrier. Whether the memo should key a call that cannot recur is a provider-admission question under std.materialization_ladder, dispatched as its own work item by the DS4.1 lane (adhoc-55498ebb-b04).",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, for the closed instance, and ONLY by measurement. No committed control pins the interpreter ROUTE: reverting either Value::Str key site in eval_recompute_arg_key or eval_recompute_value_hash back to eval_recompute_str_hash(s) leaves every committed test green. The v1-stage0-runtime rc_str_content_hash_tests pin the carrier (one hash per lineage, carried equals free) and are silent about whether the key sites read it. That is DESIGN section 3's pairing obligation unmet: deleting the integration does not make a control fail.",
    "CEILING: mechanically preventable for the route -- a control that observes how many content hashes an interpreted pure recursion over one threaded string performs, and goes red when that count scales with the step count. The accumulator instance's ceiling is set by its provider-admission ruling, not here.",
    "NEXT TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: an observation of content-hash computations that the INTERPRETER'S OWN TESTS can read -- a work-counter cargo feature in the text_lookup_work_counter pattern, or an exported accessor on RcStr -- SUFFICIENT FOR a v1-compiler test that evaluates a memoized pure recursion threading one string through many steps and goes red when a key site is reverted to rehashing. A carrier-level test in v1-stage0-runtime does not discharge it: that crate's cfg(test) is invisible to the interpreter, which is why this row exists.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    decl_ref(module_path: "v1.compiler.runtime_rust", decl_name: "rt_string_carrier"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "extdeps.languages.json.parse", decl_name: "parse_json_document"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "tools.json_parse_ladder", decl_name: "parse_96000"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "tools.json_parse_ladder", decl_name: "pass_large_text"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "tools.json_parse_ladder", decl_name: "pass_held_in_scope"),
    decl_ref(module_path: "tools.json_parse_ladder", decl_name: "accumulate_40000"),
  ],
}
